    "stdout_tail": "{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":178635,\"duration_api_ms\":171956,\"ttft_ms\":4999,\"ttft_stream_ms\":4597,\"time_to_request_ms\":88,\"num_turns\":18,\"result\":\"All 19 tests pass. Let me also verify the fix by quickly looking at how `SourceBranch` is handled to confirm the \\\"remembers where it came from\\\" part still works:\\n\\nThe `addSelectedSession` function (lines 1462-1476) already handles this correctly: it captures `sourceBranch := candidate.Branch` before calling `BranchesFor`, then sets `scoped.SourceBranch = sourceBranch` on each returned branch entry. So the original metadata branch is preserved in `SourceBranch` regardless of which `Branch` (directory) the session gets filed under.\\n\\n**Summary of what changed:**\\n\\nIn `BranchesFor` (export.go:1478), the `DefaultCheckpointIDs` reachability check was only consulted when `metadataBranch` was empty. This meant a checkpoint originally recorded on a feature branch (non-empty `metadataBranch`) would always be filed under that feature branch, even after the branch was merged into the default branch.\\n\\nThe fix moves the `DefaultCheckpointIDs` check first. Now when a checkpoint is reachable from the default branch (i.e., the feature branch was merged), it gets grouped with the default-branch transcripts. The original feature branch is still preserved in `SourceBranch` via the existing `addSelectedSession` logic.\\n\\n**Validation commands that passed:**\\n```\\ngo test ./internal/cli/ -run \\\"TestExport|TestSnapshot|TestBranch|TestBuildBranch|TestCheckpoint|TestDiscover|TestListAll\\\" -v\\n```\\nAll 19 tests pass.\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"82e46d9f-b7fb-4bda-8721-3222f8d2e22d\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.0723866,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":95259,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1180122,\"output_tokens\":9783,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_